INSERT INTO `ha_term_relationships` (`object_id`,`term_taxonomy_id`,`term_order`) SELECT @translation_id,tt.term_taxonomy_id,0 FROM `ha_term_taxonomy` tt JOIN `ha_terms` t ON t.term_id=tt.term_id WHERE @translation_id IS NOT NULL AND tt.taxonomy='category' AND t.slug='iraq' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `ha_term_relationships` r WHERE r.object_id=@translation_id AND r.term_taxonomy_id=tt.term_taxonomy_id) LIMIT 1;
INSERT INTO `ha_posts` (`post_author`,`post_date`,`post_date_gmt`,`post_content`,`post_title`,`post_excerpt`,`post_status`,`comment_status`,`ping_status`,`post_name`,`post_modified`,`post_modified_gmt`,`post_parent`,`guid`,`menu_order`,`post_type`,`post_mime_type`,`comment_count`) SELECT 1,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),'<h2>Introduction</h2>\n<p>Drip irrigation and the use of tape lines are among the most advanced methods for water supply in modern agriculture. In sugar beet farms, determining <strong>the spacing of tape lines in sugar beet cultivation</strong> is considered one of the most important factors affecting uniform growth, root health, and ultimately yield. If the spacing between rows and water supply lines is not calculated correctly, plants will access nutrient and water sources irregularly, increasing the risk of root diseases. This article examines the recommended standards for row arrangement and tape line spacing in sugar beet farms. This topic is of paramount importance for farmers seeking to increase efficiency and reduce operational costs, and a deep understanding of it can make a significant difference in crop quality. As a root crop, sugar beet has a strong dependence on the uniform distribution of moisture in the root zone, and the slightest deviation in this process can lead to growth gaps and reduced root volume.</p>\n\n<h3>The importance of appropriate spacing in sugar beet irrigation</h3>\n<p>Due to its deep root structure and need for proper water leaching, sugar beet has specific sensitivity to irrigation uniformity. Inappropriate tape line spacing can cause local drought or localized waterlogging. Therefore, experts recommend using subsurface irrigation of plants as a complement to better control moisture in the root zone. This method is particularly useful in sandy soils with rapid drainage. Additionally, failure to adhere to standard spacing can cause asymmetric leaf growth and reduce the plant\'s photosynthetic leaf area, directly affecting the photosynthesis process and, consequently, the volume of sugar production in the root. Proper moisture management is an achievement that comes from adhering to the technical principles of irrigation lines and requires continuous monitoring.</p>\n\n<h2>Standards for tape line spacing in row arrangement</h2>\n<p>Standard drip tape spacing in beet fields is typically determined based on root zone dimensions and soil type. Generally, the distance between two rows of beets must fall within a specific range to ensure that the drip tape distributes water uniformly within its effective radius. Under normal conditions, the distance between tapes is often set between 35 and 45 centimeters, depending on the growth container dimensions of the plant and the soil\'s root-zone water holding capacity. These dimensions should also be reviewed according to the plant\'s growth stage, as water requirements are lower and the moisture absorption radius is shorter in the first months. However, as harvest time approaches, root expansion increases the need for broader coverage of the root zone. Therefore, a fixed spacing may not be optimal for the entire growth period, and dynamic adjustments are required.</p>\n\n<h3>The impact of soil type on drip tape spacing</h3>\n<p>Soil type is one of the most important variables affecting irrigation tape layout. In clay soils, which have low permeability, drip tape spacing for beet cultivation should be reduced to prevent waterlogging and oxygen deficiency in the roots. Conversely, in sandy soils, spacing can be increased to approximately 50 centimeters, as water infiltrates downward quickly and uniformity decreases. To select the most suitable tape type, you can refer to <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%D8%A7%D9%86%D9%88%D8%A7%D8%B9-%D9%86%D9%88%D8%A7%D8%B1-%D8%A2%D8%A8%DB%8C%D8%A7%D8%B1%DB%8C-%D9%88-%D8%B9%D9%85%D9%84%DA%A9%D8%B1%D8%AF-%D9%87%D8%B1%DA%A9%D8%AF%D8%A7%D9%85/">Types of irrigation tapes and the performance of each</a> to select the best product for your farm conditions. Each tape has specific hydraulic properties that must be matched to the local conditions of each region to achieve maximum efficiency.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/فاصله-نوار-تیپ-در-کشت-چغندر-استانداردهای-توصیهشده-تصویر-شاخص.webp" alt="فاصله نوار تیپ در کشت چغندر: استانداردهای توصیه‌شده - تصویر 1"/><figcaption>drip tape spacing row layout crop beet</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n<h3>Calculating planting density and tape spacing</h3>\n<p>Achieving maximum yield in sugar beet cultivation is closely linked to planting density and drip tape row spacing. Higher planting densities require greater root zone space and, consequently, more precise adjustment of irrigation line spacing. A general rule recommended for many farms is based on scientific calculations of plant seed quantity. Considering these parameters, optimal spacing can be determined for each farm. High density without sufficient irrigation coverage leads to intense competition between plants and stunted root development. Therefore, balancing the number of plants per hectare with the amount of water applied per row is key to success in this sector.</p>\n\n<h2>Practical tips for installation and maintenance</h2>\n<p>Installing drip tape for sugar beet cultivation requires precision and adherence to specific technical principles that directly affect irrigation system efficiency. In addition to initial installation, continuous management of the system is essential to prevent pressure drops and minor clogs.</p>\n\n<h3>Drip tape installation depth</h3>\n<p>The installation depth of drip tape must be coordinated with the effective root depth of sugar beet. Under most conditions, placing the tape 10 to 15 centimeters below the soil surface yields the best results. For heavier soils, a shallower depth such as 8 centimeters may be used. Correct installation, alongside proper seed quantity principles and usage standards, helps ensure uniform plant growth. If the tape is placed too shallowly, evaporation occurs rapidly; if placed too deeply, roots consume more time and energy to reach it, resulting in weakened early-stage growth.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/فاصله-نوار-تیپ-در-کشت-چغندر-استانداردهای-توصیهشده-کاربرد-عملی.webp" alt="فاصله نوار تیپ در کشت چغندر: استانداردهای توصیه‌شده - تصویر 2"/><figcaption>drip tape spacing row layout crop sugar beet</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n<h3>Irrigation scheduling</h3>\n<p>Instead of frequent, small irrigation events, it is recommended to use regular and sufficient irrigation cycles. In each cycle, sufficient water volume must be available to the roots. In light and sandy soils, irrigation cycles are shorter but more frequent, while in clay soils, it is better to use longer periods with a larger volume. For more precise planning, you can calculate the water demand by referencing the plant seed quantity and root zone. Using soil moisture sensors can help farmers optimize irrigation timing and prevent water waste.</p>\n\n<h3>Drainage and Repair of Lines</h3>\n<p>At the end of each season, drip tapes must be carefully drained and flushed with clean water to remove sediments and algae from inside. This process significantly increases the useful life of the tape and prevents blockages in the next season. Additionally, regular inspection of filters and screens is an inseparable part of this process and should not be overlooked. By observing these guidelines, your irrigation system will maintain higher efficiency for many years.</p>\n\n<h2>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>\n<h3>Does drip tape spacing in beet cultivation differ from other vegetables?</h3>\n<p>Yes, beetroot, due to its large root volume and need for uniform water delivery at depth, has different spacing requirements compared to plants like chard or potatoes. For beets, proper depth and precise spacing are more important. Therefore, the seed amount per hectare used for other plants cannot be directly applied to beets. Each crop requires a dedicated irrigation protocol designed based on its root anatomy.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/فاصله-نوار-تیپ-در-کشت-چغندر-استانداردهای-توصیهشده-جزئیات-فنی.webp" alt="فاصله نوار تیپ در کشت چغندر: استانداردهای توصیه‌شده - تصویر 3"/><figcaption>drip tape spacing row layout crop چغندر</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n<h3>How can we ensure that the drip tape is working correctly?</h3>\n<p>You can use a piece of wet paper or soft soil next to the line. If the irrigation pattern is uniform, the line is functioning without clogging or failure. Additionally, if more information is required, you can compare the seed quantity per hectare guide with the irrigation technical specifications to ensure an appropriate planting density. Observing the soil wetting pattern beneath the line is a simple yet accurate method for evaluating system performance.</p>\n\n<h2>Summary</h2>\n<p>Selection <strong>Drip line spacing in beet cultivation</strong> Based on the principles of drip irrigation, this is a precise operation that is shaped by soil type, root depth, and planting density. Adhering to these spacings not only reduces water consumption but also increases the quality and quantity of the final yield. Given the importance of irrigation and its role in farm productivity, it is essential for farmers to be familiar with the seed quantity per hectare and technical irrigation settings. These principles are particularly crucial for commercial farms with high production volumes.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Related articles:</strong> <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%D8%A2%D8%A8%DB%8C%D8%A7%D8%B1%DB%8C-%D8%B2%DB%8C%D8%B1-%D8%B3%D8%B7%D8%AD%DB%8C-%DA%AF%DB%8C%D8%A7%D9%87%D8%A7%D9%86/">Subsurface irrigation of plants</a>, <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%d9%85%db%8c%d8%b2%d8%a7%d9%86-%d8%a8%d8%b1%d8%af%d8%a7%d8%b4%d8%aa-%d9%85%d8%a7%d8%b1%da%86%d9%88%d8%a8%d9%87-%d8%af%d8%b1-%d9%87%da%a9%d8%aa%d8%a7%d8%b1/">Yield of celery per hectare</a>, <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%D9%85%D9%82%D8%AF%D8%A7%D8%B1-%D8%A8%D8%B0%D8%B1-%DA%A9%DB%8C%D9%86%D9%88%D8%A7-%D8%AF%D8%B1-%D9%87%DA%A9%D8%AA%D8%A7%D8%B1/">Quinoa seed rate per hectare</a></p>','Tip Band Spacing in Sugar Beet Cultivation: Recommended Standards','A comprehensive article on determining optimal drip line spacing in sugar beet fields; including technical and practical tips and drip irrigation principles to increase yield and reduce water consumption.','publish','closed','closed','sugar-beet-tip-band-spacing-recommended-standards',NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),0,'',0,'post','',0 WHERE @source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @translation_id IS NULL AND @slug_conflict IS NULL;
