INSERT INTO `ha_term_relationships` (`object_id`,`term_taxonomy_id`,`term_order`) SELECT @translation_id,tt.term_taxonomy_id,0 FROM `ha_term_taxonomy` tt JOIN `ha_terms` t ON t.term_id=tt.term_id WHERE @translation_id IS NOT NULL AND tt.taxonomy='category' AND t.slug='iraq' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `ha_term_relationships` r WHERE r.object_id=@translation_id AND r.term_taxonomy_id=tt.term_taxonomy_id) LIMIT 1;
INSERT INTO `ha_posts` (`post_author`,`post_date`,`post_date_gmt`,`post_content`,`post_title`,`post_excerpt`,`post_status`,`comment_status`,`ping_status`,`post_name`,`post_modified`,`post_modified_gmt`,`post_parent`,`guid`,`menu_order`,`post_type`,`post_mime_type`,`comment_count`) SELECT 1,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),'<h2>Introduction: The Importance of Correct Spacing in Quinoa Cultivation</h2><p>As a low-water grain and drought-tolerant crop, quinoa has gradually established its place in sequential cropping systems in Iran. Despite its versatility and high nutritional value, this crop is highly sensitive to weather conditions and rainfall levels. In the absence of sufficient rainfall, pressurized irrigation systems, particularly drip irrigation, are the only reliable means of maintaining yield and grain quality.</p><p>One of the most significant technical challenges in quinoa cultivation is determining <strong>the correct drip line spacing</strong> . This spacing includes not only the physical distance between planting rows but also the depth of the drip line placement relative to the soil surface. Incorrect determination of these distances can lead to water stress, root growth disruption, and a noticeable reduction in crop yield. This guide examines the technical parameters for optimizing drip line layout in quinoa fields.</p><h3>Why does quinoa require precise spacing?</h3><p>Quinoa roots exhibit different vertical and horizontal spread compared to conventional rice varieties. This cereal is generally established at a shallower depth in field cropping systems. Therefore, if the drip line is placed too far from the seed line, the soil in the intermediate zone will remain dry, and lateral roots will be unable to access water. Conversely, if the spacing is too narrow, the cost of drip irrigation per hectare increases, and the risk of excess moisture and fungal growth at the plant base rises.</p><><h2>Criteria for Determining Row Spacing</h2><p>Determining quinoa line spacing is the first step in drip tape system design. This spacing affects water requirements, plant light exposure, and access to irrigation equipment.</p><h3>Standard Line Spacing</h3><p>Based on practical experience in northern and central Iran, the safe spacing for quinoa lines is generally set between 50 and 60 centimeters. This spacing allows plants sufficient room for weed expansion and natural shading until maturity. With this spacing, two quinoa plants are formed per meter of strip length, and the irrigation system with appropriate flow rates fully covers strips of 16 to 20 millimeters.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/فاصله-نوار-تیپ-در-کشت-کینوا-استانداردهای-توصیهشده-تصویر-شاخص.webp" alt="فاصله نوار تیپ در کشت کینوا: استانداردهای توصیه‌شده - تصویر 1"/><figcaption>drip tape spacing row layout crop quinoa</figcaption></figure><p>If high-yield seeds are used and the intra-line plant spacing is reduced to less than 30 centimeters, the inter-line spacing must be increased to 70 centimeters to prevent excessive weed competition and root ventilation reduction. This is critical for accelerated cropping systems.</p><h3>Impact of Tape Depth on Spacing</h3><p>The drip tape depth must align directly with the quinoa primary root spread depth. The ideal tape depth is generally 10 to 15 centimeters below the soil surface. If the tape is placed deeper than 15 centimeters, superficial quinoa roots cannot access water during early growth, causing plant stress. Conversely, if the depth is less than 5 centimeters, the tape is exposed to sunlight and mechanical damage. Therefore, precise depth adjustment, along with horizontal spacing, is key to balancing the quinoa irrigation system.</p><><h2>Determining Flow Rate and Drip Tape Type Based on Spacing</h2><p>After determining the distance between lines, you must select the drip tape type. Longer spacings require tapes with higher flow rates or closer emitter spacing.</p><ul><li><strong>16 mm tape:</strong> Recommended for line spacings of 50 to 60 cm. These tapes provide adequate coverage at flow rates of 1.5 to 2.0 liters per hour.</li><li><strong>19 or 20 mm tape:</strong> If the line spacing increases to 70 to 80 cm, use this thickness to prevent dry spots in the center of the line.</li></ul><p>The maximum distance between water outlets in the drip tape must be such that wet patches overlap. For quinoa, which has shallow roots, a 15 to 20 percent overlap in 16 mm tapes with daily irrigation frequency yields the best results.</p><h2>Practical tips for implementing quinoa drip tape systems</h2><p>Proper execution of the drip tape system requires attention to small details. Inaccuracy in connecting the tape to the main hose or during sowing can result in significant costs.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/فاصله-نوار-تیپ-در-کشت-کینوا-استانداردهای-توصیهشده-کاربرد-عملی.webp" alt="فاصله نوار تیپ در کشت کینوا: استانداردهای توصیه‌شده - تصویر 2"/><figcaption>Drip tape spacing and row layout for quinoa crops</figcaption></figure><h3>Seeding and tape installation timing</h3><p>Lay the drip tape 24 to 48 hours before sowing. Installing the tape simultaneously with seeding may cause the tape to tear and soil to clog the emitters. Also, laying the tape earlier allows for a preliminary drip irrigation cycle to moisten the seedbed, which increases quinoa germination rates.</p><h3>Consideration of land slope</h3><p>On sloped land, drip tapes should be laid perpendicular to the slope contour to prevent water accumulation on one side. If the line spacing is 60 cm, on slopes exceeding 5 percent, water may pool in the lower lines. In such cases, using tapes with biometric vents or retractable hoses can resolve the issue.</p><p>Additionally, always refer to pre-purchase considerations for drip tape and use polyethylene material with strong antioxidant protection (3-year rated tape), as quinoa is sometimes cultivated over two agricultural seasons, making chemical resistance of the tape critical.</p><h2>Frequently Asked Questions about drip tape spacing for quinoa</h2><h3>Is the drip tape spacing for quinoa the same as for corn?</h3><p>No. Corn roots are deeper, and corn row spacing is typically 80 to 90 cm. For quinoa, a spacing of 50 to 65 cm is optimal, as its roots are shallower and more sensitive to water stress.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/فاصله-نوار-تیپ-در-کشت-کینوا-استانداردهای-توصیهشده-جزئیات-فنی.webp" alt="فاصله نوار تیپ در کشت کینوا: استانداردهای توصیه‌شده - تصویر 3"/><figcaption>drip tape spacing row layout crop quinoa</figcaption></figure><h3>What should we do if drying occurs between two drip tape lines?</h3><p>If you observe dryness between two drip tape lines, increase the irrigation frequency or use tapes with higher flow rates instead of adding side tapes. Quinoa roots naturally attempt to move toward the slope of adjacent lines, but this process takes time.</p><h3>Is a spacing of less than 40 cm permissible for quinoa?</h3><p>It is not recommended. At spacings under 40 cm, the tops of the bushes intertwine, reducing air circulation between the roots. Additionally, the risk of fungal diseases at the base of the plants increases, and manual access for pest control becomes difficult.</p><h2>Conclusion</h2><p>Optimizing drip tape spacing in quinoa is a simple yet critical process. Maintaining a 50 to 70 cm distance between lines and a 10 to 15 cm depth for the tape are the main foundations for successful cultivation of this crop. By considering seed conditions, soil type, and land slope, you can prevent water waste and achieve higher grain quinoa yields. Utilizing specialized expert advice and local laboratory data is always an effective step toward successful quinoa irrigation.</p>\n<p><strong>Related Topics:</strong> <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/strawberry-yield-per-hectare-iraq/">strawberry yield per hectare iraq</a>, <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%D9%85%DB%8C%D8%B2%D8%A7%D9%86-%D8%A8%D8%B1%D8%AF%D8%A7%D8%B4%D8%AA-%D8%B3%D9%88%D8%B1%DA%AF%D9%88%D9%85-%D8%AF%D8%B1-%D9%87%DA%A9%D8%AA%D8%A7%D8%B1/">D985DB8CD8B2D8A7D986 D8A8D8B1D8AFD8A7D8B4D8AA D8B3D988D8B1DAAFD988D985 D8AFD8B1 D987DAA9D8AAD8A7D8B1</a>, <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%d8%b9%d9%85%d9%84%da%a9%d8%b1%d8%af-%d9%be%db%8c%d8%a7%d8%b2-%d8%af%d8%b1-%d9%87%da%a9%d8%aa%d8%a7%d8%b1/">Onion Performance per Hectare: Strategies to Increase Yield and Profitability</a>, <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%d9%87%d9%85%d9%87-%da%86%db%8c%d8%b2-%d8%af%d8%b1%d8%a8%d8%a7%d8%b1%d9%87-%d9%85%d8%b2%d8%a7%db%8c%d8%a7%db%8c-%d9%86%d9%88%d8%a7%d8%b1-%d8%aa%db%8c%d9%be-%d9%be%d9%84%d8%a7%da%a9%d8%af%d8%a7%d8%b1/">Everything About the Benefits of Slotted Tape</a></p>','Teejet Nozzle Spacing in Quinoa Cultivation: Recommended Standards','Quinoa requires precise irrigation scheduling under unfavorable climatic conditions. This article examines how proper drip line spacing in quinoa cultivation can affect root expansion, weed suppression, and final seed yield. Join us in reviewing technical standards for line-to-line spacing and sub-surface placement depth to prevent resource waste. The following section also covers practical tips for pre-purchase drip line trial shows.','publish','closed','closed','teejet-nozzle-spacing-quinoa-cultivation-standards',NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),0,'',0,'post','',0 WHERE @source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @translation_id IS NULL AND @slug_conflict IS NULL;
INSERT INTO `ha_postmeta` (`post_id`,`meta_key`,`meta_value`) SELECT @translation_id,'_navar_translation_queue_key','article-translation:crop-280:en-US' WHERE @translation_id IS NOT NULL AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `ha_postmeta` WHERE post_id=@translation_id AND meta_key='_navar_translation_queue_key');
